<title>USA: Handy &amp; Harman to buy Olympic Manufacturing.</title>
<headline>Handy &amp; Harman to buy Olympic Manufacturing.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Handy &amp; Harmon said Friday it has signed a letter of intent to buy Olympic Manufacturing Group Inc for $53 million and all of the shares of Olympic.</p>
<p>The transaction is expected to be completed on or about February 28, 1997.</p>
<p>It will be financed by utilizing existing unused credit facilities and the liquidation of a portion of the company's precious metal inventories.</p>
<p>Olympic will become a wholly owned unit of Handy &amp; Harmon and be part of the engineered products segment</p>
